        1. Stream Types in Java
        Java has different kinds of streams:

        Stream<T> → generic object stream (e.g., Stream<Integer>, Stream<String>).

        IntStream, LongStream, DoubleStream → primitive streams specialized for performance.

        2. Your Code
        java
        List<Integer> list = Arrays.asList(50, 70, 30, 10, 40);
        When you call:

        java
        list.stream()
        you get a Stream<Integer> (an object stream).



        3. Why mapToObj is Missing
        mapToObj exists only on primitive streams (IntStream, LongStream, DoubleStream).

